From 19099cc0323187613563b10d2cd0409112344c25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Belkin <anton.belkin@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:47:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] mac/vulkan: add --macos-sample-buffer-layer

Presents vo_gpu_next's frames through an AVSampleBufferDisplayLayer over
the Metal layer: rendered into a ring of IOSurface-backed 10-bit 4:2:0
CVPixelBuffers, imported into libplacebo as render targets, tagged with
the target color space (PQ with its mastering display and light levels;
SDR targets as sRGB, as macOS takes the swapchain's) and enqueued to be
shown at once. macOS then shows them as its own video players do, with its
HDR to SDR mapping and EDR handling. Can be switched while playing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
