+``--macos-sample-buffer-layer=<yes|no>``
+    Present frames through an ``AVSampleBufferDisplayLayer``, macOS's own video layer, instead of the
+    Vulkan swapchain (default: no). Frames are rendered as usual, into 10-bit 4:2:0 buffers tagged with
+    the target color space (``--target-trc``, ``--target-prim``, and the colorspace hint), and macOS shows
+    them as its own video players do: its HDR to SDR mapping and EDR handling instead of mpv's swapchain
+    color management. Can be changed while playing.
+    ``--vo=gpu-next`` with macOS and Vulkan (macvk) only.
+
